{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Than the voices of many waters</b> — More than the voices of many waters, which are mighty, than the breakers of the sea, which are mightier; HaShem is on high. And this is a sign that the spheres have voices, and so it is written in Ezekiel: 'like the voice of many waters.' And these voices — the deaf do not hear them, just as the blind do not perceive the works of HaShem, which are awesome."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 93, :notes {0 "The final phrase ״מעשה השם נוראים״ is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and may be elliptical for ״which are awesome.״"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:07.329124836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}